cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Building-level pluvial flood risk in Logroño under future rainfall and nature-based solution scenarios"
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
authors:
- family-names: "Fouilloux"
  given-names: "Anne"
  orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-1784-2920"
  affiliation: "LifeWatch ERIC"
repository-code: "https://github.com/annefou/logrono-flood-adaptation-scenarios"
license: MIT
version: "0.2.0"
date-released: "2026-10-11"
abstract: >-
  Building-level pluvial flood risk (social vulnerability x exposure x hazard) for
  Logroño, Spain, under the REACHOUT flood scenarios: present and future design
  rainfall (EURO-CORDEX median and 90th percentile) combined with current green cover,
  the planned nature-based solutions and an all-green city. Uses the framework of
  Vogelbacher et al. (2026) through building-climate-risk, the open city inputs of the
  Logroño replication, and checks the future rainfall against Destination Earth Climate
  DT projections and storylines. Shared analysis behind three FORRT nanopublication
  chains (future rainfall, planned nature-based solutions, who greening protects).
# Identifiers below are recorded AUTOMATICALLY on each release by
# .github/workflows/release-identifiers.yml — don't fill them in by hand.
#
# `doi:` is the CONCEPT DOI: it means "cite this project" and deliberately
# resolves to whatever version is latest. That floating behaviour is correct
# HERE and wrong in a nanopub — see scripts/set_release_identifiers.py.
#
# (This used to say "run /init-template again or edit by hand". /init-template
# deletes itself as its final step, so by the time a DOI existed the skill it
# named was gone and "edit by hand" was the only path left. Two repos built from
# this template then recorded the version DOI two different ways — one a
# structured identifier, one a prose comment. Hence the automation.)
